  "interpretation": "No CLI MapStatus observer runs in either publisher-trace trial. #267 held MapStatus ready through source stamp 25.873 s before a normalized_cost_exceeded localization lock at sim 26.335 s; telemetry/optimized/IMU were below their freshness limits at lock. #268 remained TRACKING through sim 38.479 s and MapStatus was still ready at source stamp 38.413 s. Both runs differ from #265/#266, which locked early on telemetry_stale/imu_stale while a low-bandwidth CLI observer was active, but two unpaired runs do not establish that reader load caused the difference. #268 also retained EGO odom/depth timeout reports while inputs were ready; no goal was sent, so no planner response or execution was tested.",
  "qualification": "Diagnostic only. Does not pass GOAL B/C, map geometry, EGO planning, trajectory execution, or health-threshold qualification. Thresholds remain PROVISIONAL.",
  "limitations": [
    "Two independent publisher-trace runs have different VINS epochs and observed quality-gate outcomes; CLI observer comparison is not randomized or paired.",
    "The run-local mapping logger adds low-rate file/logging work, so it is not a zero-overhead measurement.",
    "EGO stayed in WAIT_TARGET and no goal or trajectory was exercised.",
    "#267 required an Xvfb readiness signal workaround before run-live started; see startup-events.json.",
    "#268 has odom/depth lost messages in WAIT_TARGET; source identifies an EGO occupancy/input timeout but this run does not localize its downstream cause."
  ],
  "next_step": "Keep thresholds and topics unchanged. If causal attribution to MapStatus reader load is needed, run paired repetitions with and without the CLI reader under the same mapper/EGO workload while retaining the publisher-side trace; separately trace the EGO occupancy reader during an explicit no-goal baseline.",
